Agentic Code Reviewer cursor-sdk

💡 **SUGGESTION:** After a successful follow-up, returned metrics are taken only from the second AssistantMessage. The first turn — often the expensive one when reasoning/tool parts dominated — is omitted from pipeline token summaries even though its usage is logged in the retry warning.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
let metrics = assistantMessageToMetrics(response.info);
if (isRetryableIncompleteAssistant(firstInfo, firstFullText)) {
  // ... follow-up ...
  metrics = mergeAssistantMetrics(firstInfo, response.info);
}
return { /* ... */, metrics };
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: src/engine/opencode/stream.ts lines 333–355 replace `response` on retry; line 382 returns `assistantMessageToMetrics(info)` using only the final message. formatIncompleteAssistantDiagnostics (assistant-text.ts) logs first-turn tokens in the warn path but they are not merged into the returned metrics consumed by src/index.ts → provider.emitPipelineReviewOutput. 2. Scenario: First turn consumes 80k input + 40k reasoning tokens with empty text; follow-up emits JSON with 2k tokens. GitHub/ADO pipeline summaries report ~2k total, underreporting cost and making regressions in reasoning-heavy models invisible. 3. Protection: No test asserts metric aggregation across retry; opencode-assistant-text tests do not cover metrics. 4. Discards: Treating metrics as best-effort empty for OpenCode — non-retry path unchanged and SDK always exposes tokens on AssistantMessage when retry occurs, so aggregation is feasible.

**Caminhos analisados:** src/engine/opencode/stream.ts, src/engine/opencode/assistant-text.ts, src/index.ts, src/agent/metrics-display.ts
</details>

Agentic Code Reviewer cursor-sdk

💡 **SUGGESTION:** The new in-session retry orchestration in runOpencodeStream (detect incomplete assistant → send follow-up → validate) has no automated test. Only the extracted helpers in assistant-text.ts are covered, leaving the happy path and post-retry failure branches unguarded against regressions.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
// test/opencode-stream-retry.test.ts — mock sendSessionPrompt/module or stub OpencodeClient
it('retries once when first turn is reasoning-only then returns follow-up JSON', async () => {
  // first call: parts=[reasoning], fullText=''
  // second call: parts=[text:'{"reviews":[]}']
  // assert EMPTY_ASSISTANT_TEXT_CONTINUATION sent exactly once
});
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: Diff adds retry block at stream.ts lines 333–372; test/opencode-assistant-text.test.ts tests extractTextFromParts/isRetryableIncompleteAssistant/formatIncompleteAssistantDiagnostics in isolation. Grep shows no runOpencodeStream or stream.ts tests under test/. 2. Scenario: A future edit removes the second extractTextFromParts call, skips error checking after retry, or stops replacing `response` — helpers still pass while CI silently loses JSON recovery. 3. Protection: Helper unit tests do not invoke sendSessionPrompt or assert follow-up prompt text/count; AGENTS.md requires happy-path tests for behavior changes. 4. Discards: Relying on E2E seed tests — seed path does not mock OpenCode incomplete-assistant responses; cursor-sdk stream.ts is also untested but that is pre-existing and out of this diff's scope.

**Caminhos analisados:** src/engine/opencode/stream.ts, test/opencode-assistant-text.test.ts, src/engine/opencode/assistant-text.ts
</details>
